-- title:
--   Multiplicity two for corner realisations at cube-free level
-- statement:
--   Let $\mathcal O$ be a complete discrete valuation ring that is a domain of characteristic zero with finite residue field $k=\mathrm{ResidueField}(\mathcal O)$, and let $p$ be an odd prime with $p$ lying in the maximal ideal of $\mathcal O$. Let $\bar\rho$ be a residual Galois representation over $k$, that is a $k$-vector space of rank $2$ with a homomorphism from $\mathrm{Gal}(\overline{\mathbb Q}/\mathbb Q)$ to its endomorphisms factoring through a finite level, assumed absolutely irreducible (irreducible after base change to $\overline k$). Let $S,S_{\min}$ be finite sets of naturals with every element of $S$ prime, $p\in S_{\min}\subseteq S$, such that for each prime $q\neq p$ one has $q\in S_{\min}$ exactly when $\bar\rho$ fails to be unramified at $q$ (i.e. some valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ with $q$ in its nonunits carries an inertia element acting nontrivially), and such that for $q\in S_{\min}$, $q\neq p$, the adic representation attached to $\bar\rho$ is unipotent on inertia at $q$: every inertia element at a place above $q$ has characteristic polynomial $(X-1)^2$. Let $N,L$ be nonzero naturals with all prime divisors of $N$ in $S$, $p^2\nmid N$, every $q\in S_{\min}\setminus\{p\}$ dividing $N$, $q^2\mid N$ for every prime $q\neq p$ outside $S_{\min}$ dividing $N$, and $q^3\nmid N$ for all primes $q\neq p$; and with $L\mid N$, the same prime divisors as $N$, $q^2\mid N\Rightarrow q^2\mid L$, and $q^3\nmid L$ for all primes $q$. Assume weight-two cusp forms on $\Gamma_0(N)$ are $\mathbb C$-spanned by the integral lattice [`CuspForm.intLattice`](def/CuspForm_IntegralStructure.html#L3). Let $\theta$ be a ring homomorphism from the anemic Hecke algebra [`CuspForm.heckeAlgebra N 2 S`](def/CuspForm_HeckeAlgebra.html#L18) (the $\mathbb Z$-subalgebra of $\mathrm{End}_{\mathbb C}$ of these cusp forms generated by the Hecke generators away from $N$ and $S$) to $k$, satisfying: for every prime $\ell$ with $\ell\nmid N$, $\ell\notin S$, every valuation subring $P$ of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ lying over $\ell$ and every $\sigma$ that is a Frobenius at $\ell$ for $P$, the characteristic polynomial of $\bar\rho(\sigma)$ is $X^2-\theta(T_\ell)X+\ell$. Let $M$ be an abelian group that is a module over the localised Hecke algebra $T=$ [`CuspForm.heckeLocal N S 𝒪 θ`](def/CuspForm_HeckeLocal.html#L131) and over $\mathcal O$ compatibly, let $B$ be an $\mathcal O$-bilinear form on $M$ with values in $\mathcal O$, and assume [`CuspForm.heckeLocal.IsCornerRealization p ρbar N L S θ M B`](def/CuspForm_HeckeModuleCornerRealization.html#L19): there are a commuting family of operators indexed by the generators `Gen L S` acting on $H^1(L,\top;\mathcal O)$, a residual eigensystem $\bar\theta$ on those generators, an idempotent splitting of the algebra they generate, an index $i_0$ with corner ring mapping to $k$ by $\pi_k$ evaluating each generator to $\bar\theta$, the corner submodule consisting of parabolic homomorphisms, and an $\mathcal O$-linear isomorphism $e$ of $M$ with that corner submodule which matches the action of $T_\ell$ on $M$ with the cohomological Hecke operator and identifies $B$ with the pairing [`CuspForm.Bfam₀`](def/CuspForm_CornerPairingFamily.html#L140), while $\bar\theta$ agrees with $\theta$ on the $T_\ell$ for primes $\ell$ away from $N$, $L$ and $S$, vanishes on $U_q$ whenever $q^2\mid L$, and is nonzero on $U_p$ when $p\mid L$ and $\bar\rho$ is ordinary at $p$. Finally let $\mathcal O'$ be a second complete discrete valuation ring, a domain of characteristic zero with finite residue field, which is a module-finite $\mathcal O$-algebra whose structure map is local, let $\chi\colon T\to\mathcal O'$ be an $\mathcal O$-algebra homomorphism, and assume that it is not the case that $p\mid L$ while $\bar\rho$ is non-ordinary at $p$ (ordinariness meaning: above every place over $p$ there is a free rank-one submodule spanned by a basis vector, stable under the decomposition group, with inertia acting trivially on the quotient). Then the $\mathcal O$-rank of the submodule of $M$ annihilated by $\ker\chi$ equals twice the $\mathcal O$-rank of $T/\ker\chi$.
--
--   This is the multiplicity-two statement for a corner realisation at cube-free level: for each point $\chi$ of the localised anemic Hecke algebra $T$, the $\chi$-torsion part of the corner module $M$ has $\mathcal O$-rank exactly twice the rank of the order $T/\ker\chi$ it is a module over, in the case excluded from the $p$-non-ordinary situation with $p\mid L$. It is used in the level-raising step that produces new corner realisations and in the companion rank bound for corner modules.
